# tally 2.3.1 R3 (G2 fix F2, p5_b3): a pin is refused as its row would be, so `with mk = 2026-08` on a key of
# a month range `by 3` is LOAD-KEY, as the row `mk = 2026-08` is (p6_row_mk). Before: b3 2026-08.
=== p5_b3.tally
model p5
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "invented"
index ks = [k1, k2, k3]
index ys = year 2020..2030
index ms = month 2026-01..2026-12 by 3
index ns = int 1..5
input a: key ks
input yk: key ys
input mk: key ms
input nk: key ns
input y: year
ask b3: mk with mk = 2026-08
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  a = k1 "s"
  yk = 2021 "s"
  mk = 2026-04 "s"
  nk = 2 "s"
  y = 2022 "s"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KEY 2026-08 is not a key of ms (p5_b3.tally:17)
